    "description": "The hospital Management project is a web application that helps to manage the activity of hospitals Like Patient management, Doctor management, Manage appointments. Manage the records of patients and maintain the payment processes. Through this web application hospitals can store entire patients and medicinal history. \n•\tWorked with different project management methodologies like Agile, Waterfall, and Scrum. Also attended Scrum meetings. \n•\tAssisted with system migration that impacts the data flow in the applications using Java, Spring Boot, and Hibernate in collaboration with the external security team and IT infrastructure team. \n•\tConstructed REST APIs using Spring Boot, Auto-wiring, Spring Dependency Injection, and Spring MVC in order to design and develop microservices. \n•\tAutomated the creation of customer cases by the implementation of a screen scraper using Selenium and Spring MVC. \n•\tImplemented application using DAO layer, Spring Boot, and Hibernate. \n•\tAccessed and stored data using AWS cloud services, S3 and EC2.\n•\tTracked project issues and resolved issues using JIRA in an agile environment. \n•\tDeveloped front-end components using React. \n•\tAutomated provisioning, configuration management, and application deployment using Ansible. \n•\tCreated user interface (UI) and developed web applications using HTML, CSS, and Typescript. \n•\tDeveloped and designed fully functional application backend services using Python Flask. \n•\tUsed Python for handling dataset.",
